There was a bug where `.concat(C,` prop "onDismiss" would incorrectly be called
when pressing the escape or by clicking the modal overlay. The prop "onRequestClose"
should be used for this instead.

Differentiation:
- onDismiss is ONLY called when the Cancel button is pressed.
- onRequestClose is ONLY called when clicking the overlay or pressing escape.

All 3 of these modals are affected:
  - AlertModal
  - ConfirmModal
  - ReviewingChangesModal

Please make sure they all have a prop for "onRequestClose", like so:

<`).concat(C,`
  onDismiss={
    () => console.log('Cancel button was pressed.')
  }
  onRequestClose={
    () => console.log('Overlay was clicked or escape was pressed.')
  }
/>
